{"version":"1","id":"oss","handle":"oss","name":"Open Source Way","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/5b0ebeb91c344b78a2a92b8bc5956b97","description":null,"is_squad":false,"x":-4.1256,"y":0.6567,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":392,"newest_post_at":"2023-06-06T17:30:00.000Z","oldest_post_at":"2020-04-20T12:00:00.000Z","features":{"hype_score":0.006378,"listicle_ratio":0.158163,"question_ratio":0.038265,"avg_read_time":5.026316,"summary_length_avg":292.159383,"title_length_avg":46.977041,"title_length_var":162.308146,"tag_entropy":4.245724,"tag_diversity":0.459184,"top_tag_share":0.109694,"avg_upvotes":2.673469,"median_upvotes":0.0,"avg_comments":0.117347,"comment_to_upvote_ratio":0.044805,"zero_engagement_share":0.576531,"viral_share":0.002551,"posts_per_week":2.401882,"non_article_ratio":0.0,"author_present_share":0.035714,"recency_skew":0.206154},"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[1.1618,3.2941],"cadence_depth":[7.75,-2.3971],"hype_variety":[-0.5441,8.5147],"title_style":[4.4265,9.75]},"top_tags":[["open-source",119],["linux",78],["community",43],["freedos",35],["python",23],["git",20],["database",17],["tools",15]],"sample_titles":{"representative":["Write documentation like you develop code","165+ JavaScript terms you need to know","6 articles to get you excited about programming"],"outlier":["How the GDB debugger and other tools use call frame information to determine the active function calls"]},"recent_posts":[{"id":"PYS6g6oxi","title":"New developments at Opensource.com","url":"https://opensource.com/article/23/6/new-developments-opensourcecom","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/new-developments-at-opensource-com-pys6g6oxi","summary":"The internet is a network of interconnected networks, and originally it consisted of two: the military network and the academic network. Opensource.com has been supported by a commercial entity for 12 years. There are many available today, but for a long time there were only a handful of TLDs.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/14da8fa868e19d45ecff9af59778d348?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-06-06T17:30:00.000Z"},{"id":"uP7qx9WXw","title":"Tips for running virtual, in-person, and hybrid events","url":"https://opensource.com/article/23/5/virtual-in-person-events","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/tips-for-running-virtual-in-person-and-hybrid-events-up7qx9wxw","summary":"In-person events are back now, but it's important to keep in mind that virtual events didn't just come out of nowhere. Many communities held hackathons, bug and issue triaging, webinars, and so on as virtual events. A typical meetup is likely to last for 60 to 90 minutes.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/835c9675e602656cd6e9cedcf2cae225?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":2,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-05-03T07:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"nkzDN2EoA","title":"Generate web pages from Markdown with Docsify-This","url":"https://opensource.com/article/23/5/docsify-markdown-html","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/generate-web-pages-from-markdown-with-docsify-this-nkzdn2eoa","summary":"With Docsify-This, you can instantly turn any publicly available Markdown file into a responsive standalone web page. You can also link multiple Markdown files to create a simple website. Designers can alter the visual appearance of displayed pages with the point-and-click Web Page Builder interface or URL parameters.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/133690b5e072d26a6a2233780e653022?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":6,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2023-05-02T07:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"1nhvgDfS4","title":"How I used guilt as a motivator for good","url":"https://opensource.com/article/23/4/guilt-motivation","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/how-i-used-guilt-as-a-motivator-for-good-1nhvgdfs4","summary":"A conference's diversity, equity, and inclusion (DEI) initiatives required at least one speaker that does not identify as a man. I was offended; it felt like I was approached only because of my gender, not based on merit. After a few months of struggling and juggling, I can proudly say that I didn't give up.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/52ed81ea4525e818557fca6484268629?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-28T07:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"eQRTA5XHg","title":"Run a virtual conference using only open source tools","url":"https://opensource.com/article/23/4/open-source-tools-virtual-conference","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/run-a-virtual-conference-using-only-open-source-tools-eqrta5xhg","summary":"Run a virtual conference using only open source tools to run the first Creative Freedom Summit in January 2023. The event will be run virtually using Hopin, an online conference platform that isn't open source but is friendly to open source. The Fedora Design Team ran the live, weekly video calls using PeerTube.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/0574388e65a14838b4ca2da2b00edf28?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":1,"created_at":"2023-04-27T07:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"96PuZGSqQ","title":"Test your Drupal website with Cypress","url":"https://opensource.com/article/23/4/website-test-drupal-cypress","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/test-your-drupal-website-with-cypress-96puzgsqq","summary":"Cypress is an open source tool that tests anything that runs in a web browser. It's great for testing projects using front-end technologies like React and React. Cypress is so clever that when importing logic or data fixtures, you don't need to specify the file extension so you import.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/569e496b5fda07bb6b7b1b286e07b1ee?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-26T07:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"VckdP9uLJ","title":"What's new in GNOME 44?","url":"https://opensource.com/article/23/4/linux-gnome-44-features","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/what-s-new-in-gnome-44--vckdp9ulj","summary":"GNOME 44 is the standard desktop in several Linux distributions. The upcoming Fedora 38 release will include GNOME 44 and should be out sometime in April. GNOME 44 builds have already landed in openSUSE's Tumbleweed and MicroOS, to name just a few of the major distros.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/3912b598e7e6539750554ab3f043b3c2?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-25T07:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"8fTEXbk6a","title":"Learn Tcl/Tk and Wish with this simple game","url":"https://opensource.com/article/23/4/learn-tcltk-wish-simple-game","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/learn-tcl-tk-and-wish-with-this-simple-game-8ftexbk6a","summary":"Learn Tcl/Tk and Wish with this simple game. Learn Tcl by writing a simple game and Learn Expect by writing the simple game. Explore the basic language constructs of Tcl, which include user input, output, variables, conditional evaluation, simple functions and basic event driven programming.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/5443b582f6969a211e71acf6b9a44df3?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":1,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-24T07:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"KtMtZl0QF","title":"10 ways to celebrate Earth Day with open source","url":"https://opensource.com/article/23/4/celebrate-earth-day-open-source","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/10-ways-to-celebrate-earth-day-with-open-source-ktmtzl0qf","summary":"Open source brings forth many possibilities for people from all areas and levels of technical expertise. There are open source tools anyone can use to explore nature's magic, whether looking up at the night sky or down at the plants in your own backyard. Open source empowers web developers to build sustainability into their practice.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/v1/posts/1e5a06462b4b4a7d267c8358228622f4?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-22T07:00:00.000Z"},{"id":"tBt2wMuvD","title":"The future of the sharing business model","url":"https://opensource.com/article/23/4/future-sharing-business-model","comments_permalink":"https://app.daily.dev/posts/the-future-of-the-sharing-business-model-tbt2wmuvd","summary":"Arun Sundarajan calls the sharing economy \"crowd-based capitalism\" The sharing economy has five characteristics: Primarily market-based, non-hierarchical networks: Capital, assets, and labor come from decentralized crowds of individuals rather than centralized corporate or state sources. It has potentially higher and broad levels of economic activity.","image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/f_auto,q_auto/8490067e025da2b674366f36f6867315?_a=AQADKdt","num_upvotes":0,"num_comments":0,"created_at":"2023-04-21T07:00:00.000Z"}],"similar_handles":["appunite","swlh","dribbble","hackernoon","brainhub"],"opposite_handles":["felixrieseberg","tbpn","alexfinn","ryolu_","hamelhusain"],"similar":[{"id":"appunite","handle":"appunite","name":"AppUnite","is_squad":false,"x":-3.9552,"y":0.5265,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":162,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/81e132ba0ebf4c76a4960b7bec2bed76","features_preview":{"posts_per_week":0.994001,"median_upvotes":0.0,"author_present_share":0.0,"hype_score":0.015432,"avg_read_time":4.58642,"tag_diversity":0.574074},"top_tags_preview":[["general-programming",26],["flutter",18],["mobile",13]],"view_coords":{"engagement_style":[1.0441,4.4118],"cadence_depth":[1.9265,-3.3824],"hype_variety":[3.5588,7.3235],"title_style":[9.7941,8.9853]}},{"id":"swlh","handle":"swlh","name":"The Startup","is_squad":false,"x":-4.1578,"y":0.3939,"cluster_id":3,"posts_collected":311,"image":"https://media.daily.dev/image/upload/t_logo,f_auto/v1/logos/swlh","features_preview":{"posts_